{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P3dtDXjz7vhm92VN5U3jQY","type":"tool_result","content":"=== k8s/deployment.yaml\n     1\tapiVersion: v1\n     2\tkind: Namespace\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: clinic-agent\n     5\t  labels:\n     6\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\n     7\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.33\n     8\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\n     9\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted\n    10\t---\n    11\tapiVersion: v1\n    12\tkind: ServiceAccount\n    13\tmetadata:\n    14\t  name: clinic-agent\n    15\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    16\t  annotations:\n    17\t    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\n    18\t    eks.amazonaws.com/token-expiration: \"3600\"\n    19\tautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n    20\t---\n    21\tapiVersion: v1\n    22\tkind: ServiceAccount\n    23\tmetadata:\n    24\t  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n    25\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    26\t  annotations:\n    27\t    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\n    28\tautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n    29\t---\n    30\tapiVersion: v1\n    31\tkind: ConfigMap\n    32\tmetadata:\n    33\t  name: clinic-agent\n    34\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    35\tdata:\n    36\t  CLINIC_DIRECTORY: |\n    37\t    [{\"id\":\"nb-castro\",\"name\":\"Northbay Castro\",\"smsNumber\":\"+14155550110\"},\n    38\t     {\"id\":\"nb-fremont\",\"name\":\"Northbay Fremont\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550111\"},\n    39\t     {\"id\":\"nb-oakland\",\"name\":\"Northbay Oakland\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550112\"},\n    40\t     {\"id\":\"nb-sanmateo\",\"name\":\"Northbay San Mateo\",\"smsNumber\":\"+16505550113\"},\n    41\t     {\"id\":\"nb-walnutcreek\",\"name\":\"Northbay Walnut Creek\",\"smsNumber\":\"+19255550114\"}]\n    42\t  SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN: arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:418295730611:secret:clinic-agent/sms-signing\n    43\t  HTTPS_PROXY: http://egress-proxy.platform.svc.cluster.local:3128\n    44\t  NO_PROXY: ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example,.svc.cluster.local\n    45\t---\n    46\tapiVersion: apps/v1\n    47\tkind: Deployment\n    48\tmetadata:\n    49\t  name: clinic-agent\n    50\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    51\t  labels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    52\tspec:\n    53\t  replicas: 3\n    54\t  selector:\n    55\t    matchLabels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    56\t  template:\n    57\t    metadata:\n    58\t      labels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    59\t    spec:\n    60\t      serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\n    61\t      automountServiceAccountToken: false\n    62\t      hostUsers: false\n    63\t      hostNetwork: false\n    64\t      hostPID: false\n    65\t      hostIPC: false\n    66\t      enableServiceLinks: false\n    67\t      securityContext:\n    68\t        runAsNonRoot: true\n    69\t        runAsUser: 65532\n    70\t        runAsGroup: 65532\n    71\t        fsGroup: 65532\n    72\t        seccompProfile:\n    73\t          type: RuntimeDefault\n    74\t      containers:\n    75\t        - name: agent\n    76\t          image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n    77\t          ports:\n    78\t            - containerPort: 8080\n    79\t          envFrom:\n    80\t            - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n    81\t          env:\n    82\t            - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n    83\t              value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n    84\t            - name: GIT_SHA\n    85\t              value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n    86\t          securityContext:\n    87\t            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n    88\t            privileged: false\n    89\t            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n    90\t            runAsNonRoot: true\n    91\t            capabilities:\n    92\t              drop: [\"ALL\"]\n    93\t            seccompProfile:\n    94\t              type: RuntimeDefault\n    95\t          resources:\n    96\t            requests: { cpu: 250m, memory: 384Mi }\n    97\t            limits: { cpu: \"1\", memory: 768Mi }\n    98\t          readinessProbe:\n    99\t            httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 8080 }\n   100\t          volumeMounts:\n   101\t            - { name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp }\n   102\t            - { name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true }\n   103\t      volumes:\n   104\t        - name: tmp\n   105\t          emptyDir: { medium: Memory, sizeLimit: 32Mi }\n   106\t        - name: sts-token\n   107\t          projected:\n   108\t            sources:\n   109\t              - serviceAccountToken:\n   110\t                  audience: https://sts.northbay-clinics.example\n   111\t                  expirationSeconds: 900\n   112\t                  path: sts-token\n   113\t---\n   114\tapiVersion: batch/v1\n   115\tkind: CronJob\n   116\tmetadata:\n   117\t  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n   118\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n   119\tspec:\n   120\t  schedule: \"0 17 * * *\"\n   121\t  timeZone: America/Los_Angeles\n   122\t  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n   123\t  jobTemplate:\n   124\t    spec:\n   125\t      backoffLimit: 0\n   126\t      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1800\n   127\t      template:\n   128\t        metadata:\n   129\t          labels: { app: clinic-agent-reminders }\n   130\t        spec:\n   131\t          serviceAccountName: clinic-agent-reminders\n   132\t          automountServiceAccountToken: false\n   133\t          restartPolicy: Never\n   134\t          hostUsers: false\n   135\t          securityContext:\n   136\t            runAsNonRoot: true\n   137\t            runAsUser: 65532\n   138\t            runAsGroup: 65532\n   139\t            seccompProfile:\n   140\t              type: RuntimeDefault\n   141\t          containers:\n   142\t            - name: reminders\n   143\t              image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n   144\t              args: [\"dist/workers/reminders.js\"]\n   145\t              envFrom:\n   146\t                - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n   147\t              env:\n   148\t                - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n   149\t                  value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n   150\t                - name: GIT_SHA\n   151\t                  value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n   152\t              securityContext:\n   153\t                allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n   154\t                privileged: false\n   155\t                readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n   156\t                capabilities:\n   157\t                  drop: [\"ALL\"]\n   158\t---\n   159\t# Egress: DNS, the EHR MCP endpoint (private link), and the platform egress proxy only.\n   160\t# The proxy allows api.anthropic.com, the payments and SMS providers, the eligibility agent,\n   161\t# the group STS and auth service, and AWS service endpoints.\n   162\tapiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\n   163\tkind: NetworkPolicy\n   164\tmetadata:\n   165\t  name: clinic-agent-egress\n   166\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n   167\tspec:\n   168\t  podSelector: {}\n   169\t  policyTypes: [\"Egress\", \"Ingress\"]\n   170\t  ingress:\n   171\t    - from:\n   172\t        - namespaceSelector:\n   173\t            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: ingress }\n   174\t      ports:\n   175\t        - { port: 8080, protocol: TCP }\n   176\t  egress:\n   177\t    - to:\n   178\t        - namespaceSelector:\n   179\t            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system }\n   180\t          podSelector:\n   181\t            matchLabels: { k8s-app: kube-dns }\n   182\t      ports:\n   183\t        - { port: 53, protocol: UDP }\n   184\t        - { port: 53, protocol: TCP }\n   185\t    - to:\n   186\t        - namespaceSelector:\n   187\t            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: platform }\n   188\t          podSelector:\n   189\t            matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }\n   190\t      ports:\n   191\t        - { port: 3128, protocol: TCP }\n   192\t    - to:\n   193\t        - ipBlock: { cidr: 10.60.12.0/28 }\n   194\t      ports:\n   195\t        - { port: 443, protocol: TCP }\n=== infra/terraform/github.tf\n     1\t# Who can change production: only the deploy workflow running in the \"production\" or\n     2\t# \"production-emergency\" GitHub environment can assume the deploy role, and both environments\n     3\t# require a named reviewer from agent-platform-leads. Nobody else has write access to the\n     4\t# clinic-agent namespace (see access_entries in main.tf), and the cluster API is private.\n     5\t\n     6\tprovider \"github\" {\n     7\t  owner = \"northbay-clinics\"\n     8\t}\n     9\t\n    10\tdata \"github_team\" \"leads\" {\n    11\t  slug = \"agent-platform-leads\"\n    12\t}\n    13\t\n    14\tresource \"github_branch_protection\" \"main\" {\n    15\t  repository_id = \"clinic-agent\"\n    16\t  pattern       = \"main\"\n    17\t\n    18\t  enforce_admins                  = true\n    19\t  allows_force_pushes             = false\n    20\t  allows_deletions                = false\n    21\t  required_linear_history         = true\n    22\t  require_signed_commits          = true\n    23\t  require_conversation_resolution = true\n    24\t\n    25\t  required_pull_request_reviews {\n    26\t    required_approving_review_count = 2\n    27\t    require_code_owner_reviews      = true\n    28\t    dismiss_stale_reviews           = true\n    29\t    require_last_push_approval      = true\n    30\t  }\n    31\t\n    32\t  required_status_checks {\n    33\t    strict   = true\n    34\t    contexts = [\"ci / test\", \"ci / manifest-check\"]\n    35\t  }\n    36\t}\n    37\t\n    38\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production\" {\n    39\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    40\t  environment = \"production\"\n    41\t  reviewers {\n    42\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    43\t  }\n    44\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    45\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    46\t    protected_branches     = true\n    47\t    custom_branch_policies = false\n    48\t  }\n    49\t}\n    50\t\n    51\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production_emergency\" {\n    52\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    53\t  environment = \"production-emergency\"\n    54\t  reviewers {\n    55\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    56\t  }\n    57\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    58\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    59\t    protected_branches     = false\n    60\t    custom_branch_policies = true\n    61\t  }\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\tresource \"github_repository_environment_deployment_policy\" \"emergency_branches\" {\n    65\t  repository     = \"clinic-agent\"\n    66\t  environment    = github_repository_environment.production_emergency.environment\n    67\t  branch_pattern = \"hotfix/*\"\n    68\t}\n    69\t\n    70\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"deploy\" {\n    71\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    72\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    73\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    74\t    Statement = [{\n    75\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    76\t      Principal = { Federated = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com\" }\n    77\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n    78\t      Condition = {\n    79\t        StringEquals = {\n    80\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n    81\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = [\n    82\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production\",\n    83\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production-emergency\",\n    84\t          ]\n    85\t        }\n    86\t      }\n    87\t    }]\n    88\t  })\n    89\t}\n    90\t\n    91\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"deploy\" {\n    92\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    93\t  role = aws_iam_role.deploy.id\n    94\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    95\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    96\t    Statement = [\n    97\t      {\n    98\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    99\t        Action   = [\"ecr:GetAuthorizationToken\"]\n   100\t        Resource = \"*\"\n   101\t      },\n   102\t      {\n   103\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   104\t        Action   = [\"ecr:BatchCheckLayerAvailability\", \"ecr:PutImage\", \"ecr:InitiateLayerUpload\", \"ecr:UploadLayerPart\", \"ecr:CompleteLayerUpload\", \"ecr:BatchGetImage\"]\n   105\t        Resource = aws_ecr_repository.agent.arn\n   106\t      },\n   107\t      {\n   108\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   109\t        Action   = [\"eks:DescribeCluster\"]\n   110\t        Resource = module.eks.cluster_arn\n   111\t      },\n   112\t    ]\n   113\t  })\n   114\t}\n=== infra/terraform/iam.tf\n     1\t# Runtime identity for the agent pods (IRSA). This role belongs to the agent, not to any user:\n     2\t# patients and staff never receive AWS credentials, and revoking this role does not touch theirs.\n     3\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"runtime\" {\n     4\t  name                 = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n     5\t  max_session_duration = 3600\n     6\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n     7\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n     8\t    Statement = [{\n     9\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    10\t      Principal = { Federated = module.eks.oidc_provider_arn }\n    11\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n    12\t      Condition = {\n    13\t        StringEquals = {\n    14\t          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:sub\" = [\n    15\t            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent\",\n    16\t            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent-reminders\",\n    17\t          ]\n    18\t          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n    19\t        }\n    20\t      }\n    21\t    }]\n    22\t  })\n    23\t}\n    24\t\n    25\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"runtime\" {\n    26\t  name = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n    27\t  role = aws_iam_role.runtime.id\n    28\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    29\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    30\t    Statement = [\n    31\t      {\n    32\t        Sid      = \"ReadClinicSecrets\"\n    33\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    34\t        Action   = [\"secretsmanager:GetSecretValue\"]\n    35\t        Resource = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:clinic-agent/*\"\n    36\t      },\n    37\t      {\n    38\t        Sid    = \"AgentState\"\n    39\t        Effect = \"Allow\"\n    40\t        Action = [\n    41\t          \"dynamodb:GetItem\",\n    42\t          \"dynamodb:BatchGetItem\",\n    43\t          \"dynamodb:PutItem\",\n    44\t          \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\",\n    45\t          \"dynamodb:Query\",\n    46\t        ]\n    47\t        Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"\n    48\t      },\n    49\t      {\n    50\t        Sid      = \"Audit\"\n    51\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    52\t        Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]\n    53\t        Resource = aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream.audit.arn\n    54\t      },\n    55\t    ]\n    56\t  })\n    57\t}\n    58\t\n    59\t# Operators who may stop the agent. Assumable only through SSO by the on-call group.\n    60\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n    61\t  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n    62\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    63\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    64\t    Statement = [{\n    65\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    66\t      Principal = { AWS = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root\" }\n    67\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRole\"\n    68\t      Condition = {\n    69\t        StringLike = { \"aws:PrincipalArn\" = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/*/AWSReservedSSO_AgentPlatformOnCall_*\" }\n    70\t      }\n    71\t    }]\n    72\t  })\n    73\t}\n    74\t\n    75\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n    76\t  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n    77\t  role = aws_iam_role.ops_killswitch.id\n    78\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    79\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    80\t    Statement = [{\n    81\t      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    82\t      Action   = [\"dynamodb:PutItem\", \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\", \"dynamodb:GetItem\"]\n    83\t      Resource = aws_dynamodb_table.control.arn\n    84\t    }]\n    85\t  })\n    86\t}\n    87\t\n    88\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"firehose\" {\n    89\t  name = \"clinic-agent-audit-firehose\"\n    90\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    91\t    Version   = \"2012-10-17\"\n    92\t    Statement = [{ Effect = \"Allow\", Principal = { Service = \"firehose.amazonaws.com\" }, Action = \"sts:AssumeRole\" }]\n    93\t  })\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"firehose\" {\n    97\t  name = \"write-audit-bucket\"\n    98\t  role = aws_iam_role.firehose.id\n    99\t  policy = jsonencode({\n   100\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n   101\t    Statement = [{\n   102\t      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   103\t      Action   = [\"s3:PutObject\", \"s3:AbortMultipartUpload\", \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"]\n   104\t      Resource = [aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn, \"${aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn}/*\"]\n   105\t    }]\n   106\t  })\n   107\t}\n=== README.md\n     1\t# clinic-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\n     4\twidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\n     5\tsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\n     6\tvisit is covered.\n     7\t\n     8\tEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\n     9\tseparate from every other clinic's.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Components\n    12\t\n    13\t| Piece | Where | Notes |\n    14\t|---|---|---|\n    15\t| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n    16\t| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n    17\t| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n    18\t| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n    19\t| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n    20\t| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n    21\t| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n    22\t| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n    23\t| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n    24\t| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n    25\t\n    26\tThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\n    27\tthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n    28\t\n    29\t## High-impact actions\n    30\t\n    31\t`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\n    32\tthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\n    33\tretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n    34\t\n    35\t## Stopping the agent\n    36\t\n    37\tOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n    38\t`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n    39\t\n    40\t```bash\n    41\taws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n    42\t  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n    43\t```\n    44\t\n    45\tRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\n    46\trequests within 2 seconds.\n    47\t\n    48\t## Identity\n    49\t\n    50\t`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\n    51\tmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\n    52\taudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n    53\t\n    54\t## Build and test\n    55\t\n    56\t```bash\n    57\tnpm ci\n    58\tnpm run lint\n    59\tnpm test\n    60\tnpm run build\n    61\t```\n    62\t\n    63\t## Release\n    64\t\n    65\tMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n    66\t`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\n    67\treviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\n    68\ta reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n    69\t\n    70\t## Owners\n    71\t\n    72\t- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n    73\t- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`\n19:    tags = { app = \"clinic-agent\", owner = \"agent-platform\", data = \"phi\" }\n62:      instance_types = [\"m7g.large\"]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2062f5b6-954e-4243-ac14-d74aabea3af5","uuid":"aa40d4dc-f826-4e68-bc51-a57ca3704d2c","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:37:58.960Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== k8s/deployment.yaml\n     1\tapiVersion: v1\n     2\tkind: Namespace\n     3\tmetadata:\n     4\t  name: clinic-agent\n     5\t  labels:\n     6\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce: restricted\n     7\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/enforce-version: v1.33\n     8\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/audit: restricted\n     9\t    pod-security.kubernetes.io/warn: restricted\n    10\t---\n    11\tapiVersion: v1\n    12\tkind: ServiceAccount\n    13\tmetadata:\n    14\t  name: clinic-agent\n    15\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    16\t  annotations:\n    17\t    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\n    18\t    eks.amazonaws.com/token-expiration: \"3600\"\n    19\tautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n    20\t---\n    21\tapiVersion: v1\n    22\tkind: ServiceAccount\n    23\tmetadata:\n    24\t  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n    25\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    26\t  annotations:\n    27\t    eks.amazonaws.com/role-arn: arn:aws:iam::418295730611:role/clinic-agent-runtime\n    28\tautomountServiceAccountToken: false\n    29\t---\n    30\tapiVersion: v1\n    31\tkind: ConfigMap\n    32\tmetadata:\n    33\t  name: clinic-agent\n    34\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    35\tdata:\n    36\t  CLINIC_DIRECTORY: |\n    37\t    [{\"id\":\"nb-castro\",\"name\":\"Northbay Castro\",\"smsNumber\":\"+14155550110\"},\n    38\t     {\"id\":\"nb-fremont\",\"name\":\"Northbay Fremont\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550111\"},\n    39\t     {\"id\":\"nb-oakland\",\"name\":\"Northbay Oakland\",\"smsNumber\":\"+15105550112\"},\n    40\t     {\"id\":\"nb-sanmateo\",\"name\":\"Northbay San Mateo\",\"smsNumber\":\"+16505550113\"},\n    41\t     {\"id\":\"nb-walnutcreek\",\"name\":\"Northbay Walnut Creek\",\"smsNumber\":\"+19255550114\"}]\n    42\t  SMS_SIGNING_SECRET_ARN: arn:aws:secretsmanager:us-west-2:418295730611:secret:clinic-agent/sms-signing\n    43\t  HTTPS_PROXY: http://egress-proxy.platform.svc.cluster.local:3128\n    44\t  NO_PROXY: ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example,.svc.cluster.local\n    45\t---\n    46\tapiVersion: apps/v1\n    47\tkind: Deployment\n    48\tmetadata:\n    49\t  name: clinic-agent\n    50\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n    51\t  labels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    52\tspec:\n    53\t  replicas: 3\n    54\t  selector:\n    55\t    matchLabels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    56\t  template:\n    57\t    metadata:\n    58\t      labels: { app: clinic-agent }\n    59\t    spec:\n    60\t      serviceAccountName: clinic-agent\n    61\t      automountServiceAccountToken: false\n    62\t      hostUsers: false\n    63\t      hostNetwork: false\n    64\t      hostPID: false\n    65\t      hostIPC: false\n    66\t      enableServiceLinks: false\n    67\t      securityContext:\n    68\t        runAsNonRoot: true\n    69\t        runAsUser: 65532\n    70\t        runAsGroup: 65532\n    71\t        fsGroup: 65532\n    72\t        seccompProfile:\n    73\t          type: RuntimeDefault\n    74\t      containers:\n    75\t        - name: agent\n    76\t          image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n    77\t          ports:\n    78\t            - containerPort: 8080\n    79\t          envFrom:\n    80\t            - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n    81\t          env:\n    82\t            - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n    83\t              value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n    84\t            - name: GIT_SHA\n    85\t              value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n    86\t          securityContext:\n    87\t            allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n    88\t            privileged: false\n    89\t            readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n    90\t            runAsNonRoot: true\n    91\t            capabilities:\n    92\t              drop: [\"ALL\"]\n    93\t            seccompProfile:\n    94\t              type: RuntimeDefault\n    95\t          resources:\n    96\t            requests: { cpu: 250m, memory: 384Mi }\n    97\t            limits: { cpu: \"1\", memory: 768Mi }\n    98\t          readinessProbe:\n    99\t            httpGet: { path: /healthz, port: 8080 }\n   100\t          volumeMounts:\n   101\t            - { name: tmp, mountPath: /tmp }\n   102\t            - { name: sts-token, mountPath: /var/run/secrets/tokens, readOnly: true }\n   103\t      volumes:\n   104\t        - name: tmp\n   105\t          emptyDir: { medium: Memory, sizeLimit: 32Mi }\n   106\t        - name: sts-token\n   107\t          projected:\n   108\t            sources:\n   109\t              - serviceAccountToken:\n   110\t                  audience: https://sts.northbay-clinics.example\n   111\t                  expirationSeconds: 900\n   112\t                  path: sts-token\n   113\t---\n   114\tapiVersion: batch/v1\n   115\tkind: CronJob\n   116\tmetadata:\n   117\t  name: clinic-agent-reminders\n   118\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n   119\tspec:\n   120\t  schedule: \"0 17 * * *\"\n   121\t  timeZone: America/Los_Angeles\n   122\t  concurrencyPolicy: Forbid\n   123\t  jobTemplate:\n   124\t    spec:\n   125\t      backoffLimit: 0\n   126\t      activeDeadlineSeconds: 1800\n   127\t      template:\n   128\t        metadata:\n   129\t          labels: { app: clinic-agent-reminders }\n   130\t        spec:\n   131\t          serviceAccountName: clinic-agent-reminders\n   132\t          automountServiceAccountToken: false\n   133\t          restartPolicy: Never\n   134\t          hostUsers: false\n   135\t          securityContext:\n   136\t            runAsNonRoot: true\n   137\t            runAsUser: 65532\n   138\t            runAsGroup: 65532\n   139\t            seccompProfile:\n   140\t              type: RuntimeDefault\n   141\t          containers:\n   142\t            - name: reminders\n   143\t              image: 418295730611.dkr.ecr.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/clinic-agent@sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n   144\t              args: [\"dist/workers/reminders.js\"]\n   145\t              envFrom:\n   146\t                - configMapRef: { name: clinic-agent }\n   147\t              env:\n   148\t                - name: IMAGE_DIGEST\n   149\t                  value: sha256:b81f3c0e9d2a4756c8e1f0a3b2d4c6e8f0a1b3c5d7e9f1a2b4c6d8e0f2a4b6c8\n   150\t                - name: GIT_SHA\n   151\t                  value: e4b7c19d2f80a3561c7e9b0d4f2a6c8e1b3d5f70\n   152\t              securityContext:\n   153\t                allowPrivilegeEscalation: false\n   154\t                privileged: false\n   155\t                readOnlyRootFilesystem: true\n   156\t                capabilities:\n   157\t                  drop: [\"ALL\"]\n   158\t---\n   159\t# Egress: DNS, the EHR MCP endpoint (private link), and the platform egress proxy only.\n   160\t# The proxy allows api.anthropic.com, the payments and SMS providers, the eligibility agent,\n   161\t# the group STS and auth service, and AWS service endpoints.\n   162\tapiVersion: networking.k8s.io/v1\n   163\tkind: NetworkPolicy\n   164\tmetadata:\n   165\t  name: clinic-agent-egress\n   166\t  namespace: clinic-agent\n   167\tspec:\n   168\t  podSelector: {}\n   169\t  policyTypes: [\"Egress\", \"Ingress\"]\n   170\t  ingress:\n   171\t    - from:\n   172\t        - namespaceSelector:\n   173\t            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: ingress }\n   174\t      ports:\n   175\t        - { port: 8080, protocol: TCP }\n   176\t  egress:\n   177\t    - to:\n   178\t        - namespaceSelector:\n   179\t            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: kube-system }\n   180\t          podSelector:\n   181\t            matchLabels: { k8s-app: kube-dns }\n   182\t      ports:\n   183\t        - { port: 53, protocol: UDP }\n   184\t        - { port: 53, protocol: TCP }\n   185\t    - to:\n   186\t        - namespaceSelector:\n   187\t            matchLabels: { kubernetes.io/metadata.name: platform }\n   188\t          podSelector:\n   189\t            matchLabels: { app: egress-proxy }\n   190\t      ports:\n   191\t        - { port: 3128, protocol: TCP }\n   192\t    - to:\n   193\t        - ipBlock: { cidr: 10.60.12.0/28 }\n   194\t      ports:\n   195\t        - { port: 443, protocol: TCP }\n=== infra/terraform/github.tf\n     1\t# Who can change production: only the deploy workflow running in the \"production\" or\n     2\t# \"production-emergency\" GitHub environment can assume the deploy role, and both environments\n     3\t# require a named reviewer from agent-platform-leads. Nobody else has write access to the\n     4\t# clinic-agent namespace (see access_entries in main.tf), and the cluster API is private.\n     5\t\n     6\tprovider \"github\" {\n     7\t  owner = \"northbay-clinics\"\n     8\t}\n     9\t\n    10\tdata \"github_team\" \"leads\" {\n    11\t  slug = \"agent-platform-leads\"\n    12\t}\n    13\t\n    14\tresource \"github_branch_protection\" \"main\" {\n    15\t  repository_id = \"clinic-agent\"\n    16\t  pattern       = \"main\"\n    17\t\n    18\t  enforce_admins                  = true\n    19\t  allows_force_pushes             = false\n    20\t  allows_deletions                = false\n    21\t  required_linear_history         = true\n    22\t  require_signed_commits          = true\n    23\t  require_conversation_resolution = true\n    24\t\n    25\t  required_pull_request_reviews {\n    26\t    required_approving_review_count = 2\n    27\t    require_code_owner_reviews      = true\n    28\t    dismiss_stale_reviews           = true\n    29\t    require_last_push_approval      = true\n    30\t  }\n    31\t\n    32\t  required_status_checks {\n    33\t    strict   = true\n    34\t    contexts = [\"ci / test\", \"ci / manifest-check\"]\n    35\t  }\n    36\t}\n    37\t\n    38\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production\" {\n    39\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    40\t  environment = \"production\"\n    41\t  reviewers {\n    42\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    43\t  }\n    44\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    45\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    46\t    protected_branches     = true\n    47\t    custom_branch_policies = false\n    48\t  }\n    49\t}\n    50\t\n    51\tresource \"github_repository_environment\" \"production_emergency\" {\n    52\t  repository  = \"clinic-agent\"\n    53\t  environment = \"production-emergency\"\n    54\t  reviewers {\n    55\t    teams = [data.github_team.leads.id]\n    56\t  }\n    57\t  prevent_self_review = true\n    58\t  deployment_branch_policy {\n    59\t    protected_branches     = false\n    60\t    custom_branch_policies = true\n    61\t  }\n    62\t}\n    63\t\n    64\tresource \"github_repository_environment_deployment_policy\" \"emergency_branches\" {\n    65\t  repository     = \"clinic-agent\"\n    66\t  environment    = github_repository_environment.production_emergency.environment\n    67\t  branch_pattern = \"hotfix/*\"\n    68\t}\n    69\t\n    70\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"deploy\" {\n    71\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    72\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    73\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    74\t    Statement = [{\n    75\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    76\t      Principal = { Federated = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com\" }\n    77\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n    78\t      Condition = {\n    79\t        StringEquals = {\n    80\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n    81\t          \"token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub\" = [\n    82\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production\",\n    83\t            \"repo:northbay-clinics/clinic-agent:environment:production-emergency\",\n    84\t          ]\n    85\t        }\n    86\t      }\n    87\t    }]\n    88\t  })\n    89\t}\n    90\t\n    91\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"deploy\" {\n    92\t  name = \"clinic-agent-deploy\"\n    93\t  role = aws_iam_role.deploy.id\n    94\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    95\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    96\t    Statement = [\n    97\t      {\n    98\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    99\t        Action   = [\"ecr:GetAuthorizationToken\"]\n   100\t        Resource = \"*\"\n   101\t      },\n   102\t      {\n   103\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   104\t        Action   = [\"ecr:BatchCheckLayerAvailability\", \"ecr:PutImage\", \"ecr:InitiateLayerUpload\", \"ecr:UploadLayerPart\", \"ecr:CompleteLayerUpload\", \"ecr:BatchGetImage\"]\n   105\t        Resource = aws_ecr_repository.agent.arn\n   106\t      },\n   107\t      {\n   108\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   109\t        Action   = [\"eks:DescribeCluster\"]\n   110\t        Resource = module.eks.cluster_arn\n   111\t      },\n   112\t    ]\n   113\t  })\n   114\t}\n=== infra/terraform/iam.tf\n     1\t# Runtime identity for the agent pods (IRSA). This role belongs to the agent, not to any user:\n     2\t# patients and staff never receive AWS credentials, and revoking this role does not touch theirs.\n     3\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"runtime\" {\n     4\t  name                 = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n     5\t  max_session_duration = 3600\n     6\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n     7\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n     8\t    Statement = [{\n     9\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    10\t      Principal = { Federated = module.eks.oidc_provider_arn }\n    11\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity\"\n    12\t      Condition = {\n    13\t        StringEquals = {\n    14\t          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:sub\" = [\n    15\t            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent\",\n    16\t            \"system:serviceaccount:clinic-agent:clinic-agent-reminders\",\n    17\t          ]\n    18\t          \"${module.eks.oidc_provider}:aud\" = \"sts.amazonaws.com\"\n    19\t        }\n    20\t      }\n    21\t    }]\n    22\t  })\n    23\t}\n    24\t\n    25\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"runtime\" {\n    26\t  name = \"clinic-agent-runtime\"\n    27\t  role = aws_iam_role.runtime.id\n    28\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    29\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    30\t    Statement = [\n    31\t      {\n    32\t        Sid      = \"ReadClinicSecrets\"\n    33\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    34\t        Action   = [\"secretsmanager:GetSecretValue\"]\n    35\t        Resource = \"arn:aws:secretsmanager:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:secret:clinic-agent/*\"\n    36\t      },\n    37\t      {\n    38\t        Sid    = \"AgentState\"\n    39\t        Effect = \"Allow\"\n    40\t        Action = [\n    41\t          \"dynamodb:GetItem\",\n    42\t          \"dynamodb:BatchGetItem\",\n    43\t          \"dynamodb:PutItem\",\n    44\t          \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\",\n    45\t          \"dynamodb:Query\",\n    46\t        ]\n    47\t        Resource = \"arn:aws:dynamodb:${var.region}:${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:table/clinic-agent-*\"\n    48\t      },\n    49\t      {\n    50\t        Sid      = \"Audit\"\n    51\t        Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    52\t        Action   = [\"firehose:PutRecord\", \"firehose:PutRecordBatch\"]\n    53\t        Resource = aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream.audit.arn\n    54\t      },\n    55\t    ]\n    56\t  })\n    57\t}\n    58\t\n    59\t# Operators who may stop the agent. Assumable only through SSO by the on-call group.\n    60\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n    61\t  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n    62\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    63\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    64\t    Statement = [{\n    65\t      Effect    = \"Allow\"\n    66\t      Principal = { AWS = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:root\" }\n    67\t      Action    = \"sts:AssumeRole\"\n    68\t      Condition = {\n    69\t        StringLike = { \"aws:PrincipalArn\" = \"arn:aws:iam::${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}:role/aws-reserved/sso.amazonaws.com/*/AWSReservedSSO_AgentPlatformOnCall_*\" }\n    70\t      }\n    71\t    }]\n    72\t  })\n    73\t}\n    74\t\n    75\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"ops_killswitch\" {\n    76\t  name = \"clinic-agent-ops\"\n    77\t  role = aws_iam_role.ops_killswitch.id\n    78\t  policy = jsonencode({\n    79\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n    80\t    Statement = [{\n    81\t      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n    82\t      Action   = [\"dynamodb:PutItem\", \"dynamodb:UpdateItem\", \"dynamodb:GetItem\"]\n    83\t      Resource = aws_dynamodb_table.control.arn\n    84\t    }]\n    85\t  })\n    86\t}\n    87\t\n    88\tresource \"aws_iam_role\" \"firehose\" {\n    89\t  name = \"clinic-agent-audit-firehose\"\n    90\t  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({\n    91\t    Version   = \"2012-10-17\"\n    92\t    Statement = [{ Effect = \"Allow\", Principal = { Service = \"firehose.amazonaws.com\" }, Action = \"sts:AssumeRole\" }]\n    93\t  })\n    94\t}\n    95\t\n    96\tresource \"aws_iam_role_policy\" \"firehose\" {\n    97\t  name = \"write-audit-bucket\"\n    98\t  role = aws_iam_role.firehose.id\n    99\t  policy = jsonencode({\n   100\t    Version = \"2012-10-17\"\n   101\t    Statement = [{\n   102\t      Effect   = \"Allow\"\n   103\t      Action   = [\"s3:PutObject\", \"s3:AbortMultipartUpload\", \"s3:GetBucketLocation\"]\n   104\t      Resource = [aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn, \"${aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn}/*\"]\n   105\t    }]\n   106\t  })\n   107\t}\n=== README.md\n     1\t# clinic-agent\n     2\t\n     3\tPatient-scheduling agent for the Northbay Clinic Group. Patients reach it by SMS or by the web chat\n     4\twidget on each clinic's site. It looks up, books, reschedules, and cancels appointments in the EHR,\n     5\tsends SMS reminders, refunds no-show deposits, and asks the insurance-eligibility agent whether a\n     6\tvisit is covered.\n     7\t\n     8\tEach clinic is a tenant. A clinic's patients, appointments, deposits, and EHR credentials are kept\n     9\tseparate from every other clinic's.\n    10\t\n    11\t## Components\n    12\t\n    13\t| Piece | Where | Notes |\n    14\t|---|---|---|\n    15\t| HTTP service (Fastify) | `src/server.ts` | `/v1/sms/inbound` webhook, `/v1/chat` web chat |\n    16\t| Agent loop | `src/agent/loop.ts` | Claude Sonnet 4.5 snapshot, tool use |\n    17\t| Intent classifier | `src/agent/classifier.ts` | Claude Haiku 4.5 snapshot, routes emergencies and complaints to staff |\n    18\t| Tool registry | `src/tools/registry.ts` | EHR MCP server plus native tools, scanned on load |\n    19\t| Tool executor | `src/tools/executor.ts` | allowlist, kill switch, budgets, approvals, audit |\n    20\t| EHR | `src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` | MCP over streamable HTTP with mTLS, per-clinic OAuth client |\n    21\t| Payments | `src/integrations/payments.ts` | deposit refunds, provider idempotency keys |\n    22\t| SMS | `src/integrations/sms.ts` | outbound reminders and replies |\n    23\t| Eligibility peer | `src/integrations/eligibility-a2a.ts` | A2A `message/send`, token exchange per call |\n    24\t| Reminder job | `src/workers/reminders.ts` | Kubernetes CronJob, 17:00 local each day |\n    25\t\n    26\tThere is no vector store and no conversation memory. Every run starts from the patient's message and\n    27\tthe EHR. Conversation transcripts are not stored by this service.\n    28\t\n    29\t## High-impact actions\n    30\t\n    31\t`config/policy.yaml` lists the tools that need a staff approval before they run. The agent asks for\n    32\tthe approval, a front-desk lead or clinic manager approves it in the staff console, and the agent\n    33\tretries with the approval ID. Approvals expire after 15 minutes.\n    34\t\n    35\t## Stopping the agent\n    36\t\n    37\tOperators with the `clinic-agent-ops` role set `halted = true` on the `global` item (all clinics) or a\n    38\t`tenant#<clinicId>` item in the `clinic-agent-control` DynamoDB table:\n    39\t\n    40\t```bash\n    41\taws dynamodb put-item --table-name clinic-agent-control \\\n    42\t  --item '{\"pk\":{\"S\":\"global\"},\"halted\":{\"BOOL\":true},\"by\":{\"S\":\"<you>\"}}'\n    43\t```\n    44\t\n    45\tRunning work checks the flag before each model turn and each tool call, and a watcher aborts in-flight\n    46\trequests within 2 seconds.\n    47\t\n    48\t## Identity\n    49\t\n    50\t`src/agent/identity.ts` computes the agent-type-id from the image digest, harness version, prompts,\n    51\tmodel IDs, and config. Each pod also gets a random agent-instance-id at start. Both are on every\n    52\taudit record together with the accountable party, operational owner, tenant, and trace context.\n    53\t\n    54\t## Build and test\n    55\t\n    56\t```bash\n    57\tnpm ci\n    58\tnpm run lint\n    59\tnpm test\n    60\tnpm run build\n    61\t```\n    62\t\n    63\t## Release\n    64\t\n    65\tMerges to `main` need two reviews and a code owner review for prompts, config, infra, and manifests.\n    66\t`deploy.yml` builds, signs, and deploys by digest to the `production` environment, which has required\n    67\treviewers. Emergency deploys use the same workflow with `emergency: true` and must name an owner,\n    68\ta reason, and an end date; the workflow opens a follow-up review issue.\n    69\t\n    70\t## Owners\n    71\t\n    72\t- Accountable party: Northbay Clinic Group, Patient Access (VP Patient Access)\n    73\t- Operational owner: agent-platform team, `#agent-platform-oncall`\n19:    tags = { app = \"clinic-agent\", owner = \"agent-platform\", data = \"phi\" }\n62:      instance_types = [\"m7g.large\"]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01P3dtDXjz7vhm92VN5U3jQY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
