{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PdtPqBK4wyfHE5dZCZzciS","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\timport type Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n     2\t\n     3\t// Context size at decision time, in tokens.\n     4\t//\n     5\t// Counting method. Each model decision is one Messages API call. Its response usage reports the\n     6\t// prompt of that single call in three parts: input_tokens (uncached), cache_read_input_tokens, and\n     7\t// cache_creation_input_tokens. Their sum is the full prompt the model read for this decision,\n     8\t// including the part served from the prompt cache and the provider's own tool-use preamble, which\n     9\t// the provider counts but does not show. This is a per-call value, not a run or billing total.\n    10\t// We record it as \"measured\", with the cached share kept separately.\n    11\t//\n    12\t// If the response carries no usage (stream cut off, aborted call), we fall back to the\n    13\t// count_tokens estimate taken just before the call for the same request, and mark it \"estimated\".\n    14\t// If neither exists the value is null with status \"unavailable\". It is never reported as 0.\n    15\t//\n    16\t// This harness never compacts, summarizes, or truncates history inside a run, so compacted is\n    17\t// always false; a run that would outgrow its token budget stops instead (see budget.ts).\n    18\texport interface ContextSize {\n    19\t  tokens: number | null;\n    20\t  status: \"measured\" | \"estimated\" | \"unavailable\";\n    21\t  method: string;\n    22\t  cachedInputTokens: number | null;\n    23\t  compacted: boolean;\n    24\t}\n    25\t\n    26\texport const USAGE_METHOD = \"anthropic.messages.usage(input+cache_read+cache_creation)\";\n    27\texport const COUNT_METHOD = \"anthropic.messages.count_tokens(pre-call estimate)\";\n    28\t\n    29\texport async function measureBeforeCall(\n    30\t  client: Anthropic,\n    31\t  req: Anthropic.MessageCountTokensParams,\n    32\t  signal: AbortSignal,\n    33\t): Promise<ContextSize> {\n    34\t  try {\n    35\t    const r = await client.messages.countTokens(req, { signal });\n    36\t    return { tokens: r.input_tokens, status: \"estimated\", method: COUNT_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: null, compacted: false };\n    37\t  } catch {\n    38\t    return { tokens: null, status: \"unavailable\", method: COUNT_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: null, compacted: false };\n    39\t  }\n    40\t}\n    41\t\n    42\texport function completeFromUsage(pre: ContextSize, usage: Anthropic.Usage | undefined | null): ContextSize {\n    43\t  if (!usage) return pre;\n    44\t  const cacheRead = usage.cache_read_input_tokens ?? 0;\n    45\t  const total = usage.input_tokens + cacheRead + (usage.cache_creation_input_tokens ?? 0);\n    46\t  return { tokens: total, status: \"measured\", method: USAGE_METHOD, cachedInputTokens: cacheRead, compacted: false };\n    47\t}\n    48\t\n    49\t// Span attributes so the value is searchable next to the action in traces as well as audit.\n    50\texport function spanAttributes(c: ContextSize): Record<string, string | number | boolean> {\n    51\t  return {\n    52\t    ...(c.tokens === null ? {} : { \"clinic_agent.context.tokens\": c.tokens }),\n    53\t    \"clinic_agent.context.status\": c.status,\n    54\t    \"clinic_agent.context.method\": c.method,\n    55\t    \"gen_ai.conversation.compacted\": c.compacted,\n    56\t  };\n    57\t}\nsrc/tools/executor.ts:6:import { AGENT_INSTANCE_ID, type RunContext } from \"../agent/identity.js\";\nsrc/tools/executor.ts:72:        agentInstanceId: AGENT_INSTANCE_ID,\nsrc/tools/approvals.ts:15:  agentInstanceId: string;\nsrc/tools/approvals.ts:36:  agentInstanceId: string;\nsrc/tools/approvals.ts:47:    agentInstanceId: req.agentInstanceId,\nsrc/audit/recorder.ts:13:  agentInstanceId: z.string().uuid(),\nsrc/server.ts:4:import { computeAgentTypeId, setAgentTypeId, AGENT_INSTANCE_ID } from \"./agent/identity.js\";\nsrc/server.ts:37:app.log.info({ agentTypeId: typeId, agentInstanceId: AGENT_INSTANCE_ID, release: manifest.release }, \"starting\");\n119:  async recordUsage(u: Usage, model: string): Promise<void> {\n120:    const price = this.b.pricingUsdPerMTok[model];\n121:    if (!price) throw new Error(`no pricing for model ${model}`);\n     1\t# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7\n     2\tFROM node:22.11-bookworm-slim@sha256:3f1a8d2c9b7e4f6a5d0c8b1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a AS build\n     3\tWORKDIR /app\n     4\tCOPY package.json package-lock.json ./\n     5\tRUN npm ci --ignore-scripts\n     6\tCOPY tsconfig.json ./\n     7\tCOPY src ./src\n     8\tRUN npm run build && npm prune --omit=dev\n     9\t\n    10\tFROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot@sha256:9b2e4c6a8d0f1e3c5a7b9d1f3e5c7a9b1d3f5e7c9a1b3d5f7e9c1a3b5d7f9e1c\n    11\tWORKDIR /app\n    12\tENV NODE_ENV=production \\\n    13\t    CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT=/app\n    14\tCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/node_modules ./node_modules\n    15\tCOPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/dist ./dist\n    16\tCOPY --chown=65532:65532 package.json ./\n    17\tCOPY --chown=65532:65532 prompts ./prompts\n    18\tCOPY --chown=65532:65532 config ./config\n    19\tCOPY --chown=65532:65532 release ./release\n    20\tUSER 65532:65532\n    21\tEXPOSE 8080\n    22\tCMD [\"dist/server.js\"]\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"name\": \"clinic-agent\",\n     3\t  \"version\": \"3.4.1\",\n     4\t  \"private\": true,\n     5\t  \"type\": \"module\",\n     6\t  \"engines\": {\n     7\t    \"node\": \">=22.11\"\n     8\t  },\n     9\t  \"scripts\": {\n    10\t    \"build\": \"tsc -p tsconfig.json\",\n    11\t    \"start\": \"node dist/server.js\",\n    12\t    \"reminders\": \"node dist/workers/reminders.js\",\n    13\t    \"lint\": \"eslint src test\",\n    14\t    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\n    15\t  },\n    16\t  \"dependencies\": {\n    17\t    \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\": \"0.65.0\",\n    18\t    \"@aws-sdk/client-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n    19\t    \"@aws-sdk/client-firehose\": \"3.893.0\",\n    20\t    \"@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager\": \"3.893.0\",\n    21\t    \"@aws-sdk/lib-dynamodb\": \"3.893.0\",\n    22\t    \"@modelcontextprotocol/sdk\": \"1.18.2\",\n    23\t    \"fastify\": \"5.6.1\",\n    24\t    \"jose\": \"6.1.0\",\n    25\t    \"pino\": \"9.11.0\",\n    26\t    \"undici\": \"7.16.0\",\n    27\t    \"yaml\": \"2.8.1\",\n    28\t    \"zod\": \"3.25.76\"\n    29\t  },\n    30\t  \"devDependencies\": {\n    31\t    \"@types/node\": \"22.18.6\",\n    32\t    \"eslint\": \"9.36.0\",\n    33\t    \"typescript\": \"5.9.2\",\n    34\t    \"typescript-eslint\": \"8.44.1\",\n    35\t    \"vitest\": \"3.2.4\"\n    36\t  }\n    37\t}\n\n## C01 · G2 · C1–C6/Obs-T1 — Complete release manifest\n\n**Lead:** Agent team. **Shares:** Infrastructure, Model team, Data and privacy.\n\n### Requirement\n\nWrite a release manifest: a list of everything that makes up this release. Include the container, harness, system prompt, rules files, model, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval settings, identity bindings, network rules, and execution budgets. Include security-policy versions, MCP protocol and extension versions, approved tool-publication config, issuer/audience bindings, and cache/task isolation settings. Add a separate model record for every model: the main agent model, sub-agent models, and helper models such as embedding models and rerankers. For each, record the provider, model ID, exact version or checkpoint, and any adapter or fine-tune version. For training or fine-tuning you run yourself, also record the training job ID, base-model version, training code and config version, dataset version, and the digest of the output. The agent app's release number alone is not enough. Use the [model provenance fields](CHECKLIST-VERIFICATION.md#model-provenance-fields) to separate recorded versions from details a provider doesn't share. Check each model ID you request against the provider's versioning docs. Mark it as a pinned snapshot or as an alias that can change, and record which doc you used and its date. Naming rules differ by provider and model generation. Name each artifact's owner and a reference that can't change, where one exists. A machine-readable format, such as CycloneDX ML-BOM or the SPDX 3.0 AI and Dataset profiles, lets tools check the manifest.\n\n  Why this is hard: Teams can usually find their own training jobs and datasets. A hosted provider may not share its pretraining runs, weights, or data versions. Separate the records your team should have from the details the provider keeps private.\n\n  If you can't fully do it: Fill in model records from serving metadata, registries, and training-job output. Require full history for training your team runs. Clearly label fields the provider hides, and keep where and when you checked. Prefer a fixed provider snapshot when one exists. Record missing training history your team should have as a Gap, and rebuild it first. Never make up training versions. Never treat a provider alias as a training job ID.\n\n  Tradeoffs you can accept: Provider pretraining details that are clearly marked as not shared, as long as your own model-selection and training records are complete. A G2 gap in visibility or history can get written acceptance with an owner. Unknown records must never be written down as real versions.\n\n### Verification recipe\n\nExport the deployed artifacts and settings, and match them field by field against the manifest. Check MCP protocol/extension versions, approved tool-publication and policy/config versions, issuer/audience bindings, and cache/task isolation against deployment. Fill in the provenance fields above for every model role. For each training job you ran, follow its output digest to the served checkpoint or adapter. Separate fields the provider doesn't share from records your team is missing. Check each requested model ID's snapshot-or-alias label against the cited provider doc.\n\n**Evidence to keep:** Manifest-vs-deployment diff, model registry records, training jobs, dataset versions.\n\n### Checks for likely_pass\n\nRate likely_pass only if every check below is true, with a file and line for each:\n\n- **C01.1** A release manifest file lists the container, harness, system prompt, rules files, model, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval settings, identity bindings, network rules, execution budgets, and security-policy versions. *(A document can show this.)*\n  - *How to verify:* 1) Find the release manifest (`.brace/manifest.yaml`, release manifest, ML-BOM). 2) Check each category: container, harness, system prompt, rules files, model, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval, identity bindings, network rules, budgets, security-policy versions. 3) Compare with what config sets up (`*.mcp.json`, NetworkPolicy). 4) Answer no if any category is missing or configured items are left out.\n- **C01.2** The manifest has a separate model record for every model (main, sub-agent, and helper models such as embedding models and rerankers), each with provider, model ID, exact version or checkpoint, and adapter or fine-tune version. *(A document can show this.)*\n  - *How to verify:* 1) Search code for every model used: main, sub-agent, embedding, reranker, judge. 2) Check the manifest has a separate record for each. 3) Check each record has provider, model ID, exact version or checkpoint, and adapter or fine-tune version. 4) Answer no if any model in code has no record, or a record is missing a field.\n- **C01.3** Each requested model ID is labeled as a pinned snapshot or a changeable alias, with the provider doc and date used.\n  - *How to verify:* 1) Open each model record in the manifest. 2) Check it has a pinned-or-alias label, the provider doc used, and a date. 3) Answer no if any record lacks one of these, or labels an undated or `-latest` name as pinned.\n- **C01.4** Each artifact has a named owner and a reference that can't change (digest or commit) where one exists, not a mutable tag or the app's release number.\n  - *How to verify:* 1) For each manifest artifact, check for a named owner. 2) Check its reference is a digest (`sha256:`) or commit SHA where one exists. 3) Answer no if any artifact has no owner, or uses a mutable tag (`:latest`, branch name) or the app release number where a digest or commit was available.\n- **C01.5** For training the team runs itself, the manifest records the training job ID, base-model version, training code and config version, dataset version, and output digest.\n  - *How to verify:* 1) Search for training or fine-tuning code (training jobs, `Trainer`, fine-tune API calls, pipeline configs). 2) If found, check the manifest records job ID, base-model version, training code and config version, dataset version, and output digest. 3) Answer no if training runs here and any field is missing. Answer unknown if training may run in another repo.\n\n### Not covered here\n\nFile these problems under their owning item, not this one, unless this item's own requirement is also broken:\n\n- Running setup not checked against the approved manifest → **C03**\n- Manifest changes made without a reviewed diff and named author → **C02**\n- Running config drifting from the approved baseline unnoticed → **C04**\n- Agent-type-id not computed as a hash of its identity inputs → **A03**\n\n### Heuristics\n\n**Provable from code:** partly\n\n**Look for:**\n- A release manifest file listing container digest, harness version, system prompt and rules files, built-in tools, MCP servers, permission scopes, memory and retrieval settings, identity bindings, network rules, execution budgets, and security-policy versions.\n- A separate model record for each model role (main, sub-agent, judge, embedding, reranker) with provider, requested model ID, exact version or checkpoint, and adapter or fine-tune version.\n- Each requested model ID marked as pinned snapshot or changeable alias, with the provider doc and date cited.\n- For self-run training: job ID, base-model version, training code and config version, dataset version, and output digest.\n- Owners named per artifact, and immutable references (digests, commit SHAs) where they exist; optionally a CycloneDX ML-BOM or SPDX 3.0 AI profile.\n\n**Red flags:**\n- Only an app version number or git tag identifies the release.\n- Helper models (embedding, reranker, judge) are missing from the manifest.\n- Provider alias written into a training job or version field, or made-up version values where the provider shares none.\n- MCP servers, egress rules, or budgets are configured but not listed in the manifest.\n- Model ID recorded with no pinned-or-alias label.\n\n**Where to look:**\n- .brace/manifest.yaml, release manifests, SBOM/ML-BOM files (`*.cdx.json`, `bom.json`)\n- model config files and env vars that set model IDs\n- *.mcp.json, agent config, k8s NetworkPolicy, Helm values\n- training pipeline configs and model registry references\n\n**Needs runtime evidence:** Code shows what the manifest declares. Proving it matches the deployment needs the C01 recipe: export deployed artifacts and settings and diff them field by field, and follow training outputs to the served checkpoint.\n\n**N/A when:** never\n\n## C02 · G2 · C1–C7 — Review security-relevant changes","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2062f5b6-954e-4243-ac14-d74aabea3af5","uuid":"d39524ca-86fe-42f3-8929-63c05158684a","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:38:34.202Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\timport type Anthropic from \"@anthropic-ai/sdk\";\n     2\t\n     3\t// Context size at decision time, in tokens.\n     4\t//\n     5\t// Counting method. Each model decision is one Messages API call. Its response usage reports the\n     6\t// prompt of that single call in three parts: input_tokens (uncached), cache_read_input_tokens, and\n     7\t// cache_creation_