ual edits.\n- IAM or RBAC that limits who can change production config, prompts, and network policy.\n- A documented emergency-change path that records owner, reason, end date, and follow-up review.\n\n**Red flags:**\n- Prompts or tool lists loaded from a database, admin UI, or feature-flag service that anyone with app access can edit without review.\n- CODEOWNERS or required reviews missing for prompt, policy, or MCP config paths.\n- Deploy scripts or `kubectl apply` run from laptops with broad production credentials.\n- Break-glass access with no expiry or no follow-up record.\n\n**Where to look:**\n- CODEOWNERS, branch protection settings, `.github/workflows` or other CI configs\n- prompt storage (files vs database vs remote prompt registry)\n- IAM/RBAC for deploy roles; GitOps config (Argo CD, Flux)\n- change-management or break-glass docs\n\n**Needs runtime evidence:** Needs the C02 recipe: try changing a prompt, tool, and network policy with a role lacking release permission and see each denied, and review real normal and emergency change records.\n\n**N/A when:** never\n\n8:    bucket         = \"northbay-tfstate-418295730611\"\n48:  access_entries = {\n133:# Audit: Firehose to an S3 bucket with object lock in compliance mode (7 years, HIPAA retention).\n134:resource \"aws_s3_bucket\" \"audit\" {\n135:  bucket              = \"clinic-agent-audit-${data.aws_caller_identity.current.account_id}\"\n139:resource \"aws_s3_bucket_object_lock_configuration\" \"audit\" {\n140:  bucket = aws_s3_bucket.audit.id\n149:resource \"aws_kinesis_firehose_delivery_stream\" \"audit\" {\n150:  name        = \"clinic-agent-audit\"\n154:    bucket_arn          = aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn\n155:    prefix              = \"audit/dt=!{timestamp:yyyy-MM-dd}/\"\n156:    error_output_prefix = \"audit-errors/!{firehose:error-output-type}/\"\n{\n  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n  \"repo\": \"\",\n  \"commit\": null,\n  \"reviewed_at\": \"2026-10-20T12:36:56Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"TODO: what was reviewed and what wasn't.\",\n  \"review_protocol\": \"coverage-first-v1\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"item\": \"A05\",\n      \"gate\": \"G1\",\n      \"title\": \"Operational lookup\",\n      \"requirement\": \"Start from one suspicious action. Find the team responsible, the current operator, the deployment manifest, and the live instance. Show that you can contain the right instance or agent type without cutting off the launching user's other access.\",\n      \"not_covered\": [\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool streams within a set time\",\n          \"owner\": \"R11\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"No drill for a compromised shared tool or agent type\",\n          \"owner\": \"E12\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"problem\": \"Action records missing any of the six identity fields\",\n          \"owner\": \"A02\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"rating\": \"needs_evidence\",\n      \"confidence\": \"low\",\n      \"evidence\": [],\n      \"checks\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"A05.1\",\n          \"check\": \"Each audit record carries the agent-type-id and agent-instance-id, which resolve to a stored deployment manifest and a live instance.\",\n          \"verify\": \"1) Open the audit record writer. 2) Check `agent.type.id` and `agent.instance.id` are written on every record. 3) Check the type ID can be looked up to a stored manifest (registry, manifest store, file keyed by hash). 4) Answer no if either field is missing or nothing stores manifests by that ID. Answer unknown if the lookup store is outside this repo.\",\n          \"met\": \"unknown\",\n          \"evidence\": \"\",\n          \"quote\": \"\",\n          \"counter_search\": \"\",\n          \"note\": \"\",","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GTEAmUnkha7tZYVWWGVY9J","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type"