{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FBDhZwFneZnPcYvGrv4djw","type":"tool_result","content":"Saved A06.1 = no. Next: A06.2 — Each sub-agent's records include its direct parent's instance ID and a trace link to the parent.\n  How to verify: 1) Open sub-agent spawn code and the child's record writer. 2) Look for a parent instance field (for example `agent.parent.instance_id`) and trace propagation (span parent, span link, `traceparent` in queued payloads). 3) Answer no if any spawn path, including remote or queued, starts a fresh trace or omits the parent ID.\nSaved A06.2 = no. Next: A06.3 — The prompt the parent passed to the child is captured on this path, with prompt capture switched on in config rather than left at the default off.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where the parent's prompt to the child is recorded (for example `agent.parent.prompt`, or a hash plus stored text). 2) Check prompt content capture is turned on in config, for example a GenAI capture-content env var or SDK option. 3) Answer no if capture is left at its default off, or the setting falls back to false when unset.\nSaved A06.3 = no. Next: A06.4 — Captured prompt text is stored with restricted access and a redaction policy, and only an approved audit role can read it.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where captured prompt text is stored (bucket, table, log index). 2) Check its IAM or ACL limits reads to an approved audit role. 3) Check a redaction policy is defined and applied. 4) Answer no if prompts go to general logs the whole team can read, or no redaction exists. Answer unknown if storage access is set outside this repo.\nSaved A06.4 = unknown. Next: finish item A06 with `answer.py ... item A06 --rating ...`\nAdded red flag to A06.\nSaved item A06 = gap. Next: A07.1 — A model inventory in code or config lists every helper model the agent calls (verifiers, judges, rerankers, embedding models, world models).\n  How to verify: 1) Search for every model call: provider SDK clients, model name strings, embedding, rerank, moderation, and judge calls. 2) Compare that list with the model inventory. 3) Answer no if any helper model called in code is missing from the inventory, or no inventory exists.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2062f5b6-954e-4243-ac14-d74aabea3af5","uuid":"0f1434ad-5b99-4dcb-955d-93e8149c8fd4","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:40:36.005Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Saved A06.1 = no. Next: A06.2 — Each sub-agent's records include its direct parent's instance ID and a trace link to the parent.\n  How to verify: 1) Open sub-agent spawn code and the child's record writer. 2) Look for a parent instance field (for example `agent.parent.instance_id`) and trace propagation (span parent, span link, `traceparent` in queued payloads). 3) Answer no if any spawn path, including remote or queued, starts a fresh trace or omits the parent ID.\nSaved A06.2 = no. Next: A06.3 — The prompt the parent passed to the child is captured on this path, with prompt capture switched on in config rather than left at the default off.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where the parent's prompt to the child is recorded (for example `agent.parent.prompt`, or a hash plus stored text). 2) Check prompt content capture is turned on in config, for example a GenAI capture-content env var or SDK option. 3) Answer no if capture is left at its default off, or the setting falls back to false when unset.\nSaved A06.3 = no. Next: A06.4 — Captured prompt text is stored with restricted access and a redaction policy, and only an approved audit role can read it.\n  How to verify: 1) Find where captured prompt text is stored (bucket, table, log index). 2) Check its IAM or ACL limits reads to an approved audit role. 3) Check a redaction policy is defined and applied. 4) Answer no if prompts go to general logs the whole team can read, or no redaction exists. Answer unknown if storage access is set outside this repo.\nSaved A06.4 = unknown. Next: fin