ency deploy, assigned to the owner, with commit and approval run id.\"},\n {\"subject\":\"branch and approval for emergency\",\"status\":\"enforced\",\"evidence\":\".github/workflows/deploy.yml:51\",\"quote\":\"[[ \\\"$GITHUB_REF_NAME\\\" == hotfix/* ]] || { echo \\\"emergency deploys come from hotfix/* branches\\\"; exit 1; }\",\"note\":\"Emergency path is limited to hotfix branches and the production-emergency environment with a required reviewer.\"}\n]\nE\ncd ../agent; P=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; a() { $P ../skill/scripts/answer.py brace-findings.json \"$@\"; }\nfor c in 1 2 3; do $P ../skill/scripts/review_coverage.py ledger brace-findings.json C02.$c --rows ../scratch/C02$c.rows.json --deviations ../scratch/empty.json --attempts ../scratch/empty.json; done\na check C02.1 --met yes --evidence infra/terraform/github.tf:26 --quote 'required_approving_review_count = 2' --counter \"Searched for prompts, tools, policy or manifest loaded from a database, URL, flag service or untracked path (grep loadYaml, readFileSync, fetch in src): none; checked CODEOWNERS and branch protection cover /prompts, /config, /release. The snapshot has no .git, so tracking is inferred from the repo layout.\" --note \"Two reviews plus code-owner review, enforced for admins.\" | head -1\na check C02.2 --met yes --evidence .github/workflows/deploy.yml:37 --quote \"environment: \\${{ inputs.emergency && 'production-emergency' || 'production' }}\" --counter \"Looked for a deploy path outside the protected environments, a broad group or the agent's own credentials with cluster write access, and kubectl from laptops: only the deploy role has an access entry and it is assumable only from the two environments. The catch-all '*' owner cannot ship to production without leads approval.\" --note \"Named reviewer team gates both environments.\" | head -1\na check C02.3 --met yes --evidence .github/workflows/deploy.yml:92 --quote '--label emergency-change,needs-review \\' --counter \"Looked for an emergency path missing owner, reason, end date or follow-up, or one that skips the protected environment: all four are required and recorded; the date is only checked for format, not for being near-term.\" --note \"Owner, reason, end date and follow-up issue are all recorded.\" | head -1\n"}}}
