{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDWQKLieTstrRZ4rr5MZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed A05, A06, A07, C01 and C02. The findings are saved in `agent/brace-findings.json`. Validation with `--batch A05,A06,A07,C01,C02 --before-challenges --fix` printed `Valid` (3 gaps, 1 likely_pass, 1 needs_evidence). I did not run challenges.\n\nI ran the pre-scan and the inventory. The inventory covered both model call sites, the audit writers, and the tool registration paths. The pre-scan left 11 hits unresolved, none of them for these five items. The validator did not require them, so I left them for the batches that own them:\n- **R13:** H006–H010, audit write inside a `try` block.\n- **B11:** H001–H004, `securityContext` checks.\n- **B02:** H005, wildcard IAM grant.\n- **E03:** H011, tool list loaded from the server.\n\n| Item | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| A05 Operational lookup | **gap** (medium confidence) | The stop control only works at global or per-clinic level. Nothing can contain one instance or one agent type (`src/control/kill-switch.ts:57-58`). The IRSA role is also shared by the agent and the reminders job. Checks A05.1 and A05.2 are `unknown`: the instance-to-pod mapping and the on-call rotation are not in code. |\n| A06 Parent and prompt provenance | **gap** (medium confidence) | The A2A eligibility call forwards `traceparent`, but it gives the peer no ID of its own and sends no parent instance ID. The request is not captured in the audit event (`src/workflows/eligibility-check.ts:35`). |\n| A07 Every model in the loop | **needs_evidence** | The classifier is pinned, hashed with its prompt and config, logged on every outcome, and routes to staff on timeout, version mismatch, bad output or low confidence. A07.1 is `unknown` because the eligibility peer's model is not inventoried, and that peer's answer can trigger a refund. |\n| C01 Release manifest | **gap** (high confidence) | The manifest has no issuer/audience bindings, MCP or tool-publication settings, or cache/task isolation settings. Most artifacts have no owner. The allowlist, budgets and policy are listed by path with no digest. C01.2 is `unknown` for the same peer reason as A07.1. |\n| C02 Review security-relevant changes | **likely_pass** (medium confidence) | Two reviews plus code-owner review are enforced, and the deploy role is limited to the two protected environments. The emergency path requires an owner, a reason, an end date and a follow-up issue. This is not challenge-sealed. |\n\nTwo things to know:\n- **A06 judgment call:** I treated the A2A peer as a delegated agent task, since the skill lists A2A task creation under sub-agent spawning. If governance rules it is not a sub-agent, A06 becomes an N/A candidate instead of a gap.\n- **No `.git` metadata:** The snapshot has no `.git`, so C02.1's \"tracked in git\" is inferred from the repo layout and the Terraform branch protection.\n\nI ran the skill scripts without `-I` because `review_coverage.py` needs to import its sibling `prescan.py`. The scripts are the supplied ones and I never ran the repo's code. The ledger and rows files are in `scratch/`, next to `agent/`. The pre-scan and inventory outputs are in `agent/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1114,"cache_read_input_tokens":121169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1114},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2062f5b6-954e-4243-ac14-d74aabea3af5","uuid":"173a4a1b-7747-46c7-a34b-9d73d374b8c0","timestamp":"2026-10-20T12:42:51.509Z","request_id":"req_011CgDWQK47C7hDPDKeM3BML"}
